---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
---

<Layout title="Scott Okamoto - Portfolio">
  <section id="home" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="text-center pt-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3 tracking-tight">
        Scott Okamoto
      </h1>

      <p class="text-accent-blue text-sm font-medium tracking-wide uppercase">
        Full-stack developer focused on server-first systems and backend-heavy applications
      </p>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-lg leading-relaxed">
        I build backend-driven web applications focused on persistent state and system design.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mt-8 justify-center">
        <a href="#projects"
          class="bg-accent-blue hover:bg-blue-400 text-black font-medium px-6 py-3 rounded-lg transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-[0_0_12px_theme(colors.accent.blue/25%)] text-center sm:min-w-[140px]">
          View Projects
        </a>
        <a href="#contact"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 border border-border-subtle hover:border-accent-blue px-6 py-3 rounded-lg transition-all duration-200 text-center sm:min-w-[140px]">
          Contact
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects" class="bg-bg-surface max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      Projects
    </h2>
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-2">
      <ProjectCard 
        title="Relay RPG"
        description="Event-driven Discord RPG where game state, character data, and turn progression are 
        managed through server-side logic. Players interact through commands that update persistent SQLite-backed state."
        tech={["Node.js", "SQLite", "Discord SDK", "Fly.io"]}
        github="https://github.com/swokamoto/relay-rpg"
        designDoc="https://github.com/swokamoto/system-design-notes/blob/main/relay-rpg.md"
      />
      <ProjectCard 
        title="Isabelle's Bead Shop"
        description="Full-stack e-commerce system with an admin dashboard for inventory and order management, 
        including Stripe-based checkout and customer review workflows."
        tech={["React", "Node.js", "Stripe", "MongoDB"]}
        github="https://github.com/hannah-finch/isabelles-bead-shop"
        live="https://isabellesbeadshop.onrender.com/"
      />
      <ProjectCard 
        title="Zen Garden"
        description="Server-backed application where users modify persistent garden state stored in PostgreSQL. 
        The system translates structured data into SVG-based visual output."
        tech={["Node.js", "PostgreSQL", "Sequelize", "SVG"]}
        github="https://github.com/swokamoto/zenGarden2"
        live="https://zengarden-5q63.onrender.com/"
        designDoc="https://github.com/swokamoto/system-design-notes/blob/main/zen-garden.md"
      />
      <!-- <ProjectCard 
        title="PokeLounge"
        description="Interactive ambient web app where users add up to 4 Pokémon to a cozy scene via the PokéAPI, drag-and-drop them between seats, and relax to a built-in lofi music player. Pokémon selections persist across sessions via localStorage, scenes are swappable, and each Pokémon generates a Chuck Norris joke with their name swapped in via a second API."
        tech={["JQuery", "JavaScript", "HTML", "CSS"]}
        github="https://github.com/swokamoto/group-11-project-pokemon"
        live="https://group11projectpokemon.github.io/group-11-project-pokemon/"
      /> -->
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="process" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      How I Build
    </h2>
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">Model the system first</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">I start by defining how data is structured and how it changes over time before writing code.
        In Relay RPG, this meant designing character state and turn flow before implementing any commands.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">State over UI</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">I focus on how information is stored and updated rather than how it is displayed.
        Applications become predictable when state is clearly defined and centrally managed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">Clear domain APIs</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">I design APIs around the behavior of the system, not the shape of the UI.
        This keeps backend logic reusable and easier to evolve.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">Design for failure</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">I build systems that handle broken dependencies, invalid input, and edge cases gracefully
        to ensure predictable behavior under real-world conditions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="bg-bg-surface max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      About
    </h2>
    <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-2xl p-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <div class="space-y-4 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-center">
        <p>
          I'm a full-stack developer focused on backend systems, persistent state, and predictable application behavior.
        </p>

        <p>
          Before software, I spent 10 years as a Helicopter Crew Chief in the Air Force — where system reliability and structured troubleshooting weren't optional. I carry that same approach into how I design and build software.
        </p>

        <p>
          My work spans multiplayer Discord bots, e-commerce platforms, and database-backed tools, all centered on server-managed state and consistent data flow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      Contact
    </h2>
    <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-2xl p-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-center mb-6">
        Open to full-time and contract opportunities in backend or full-stack development.
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-6">
          <span class="text-text-muted text-sm">Email</span>
          <a href="mailto:swokamoto@gmail.com" class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 transition-all duration-200">swokamoto@gmail.com</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-6">
          <span class="text-text-muted text-sm">LinkedIn</span>
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/sokamoto" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 transition-all duration-200">linkedin.com/in/sokamoto</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-6">
          <span class="text-text-muted text-sm">GitHub</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/swokamoto" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 transition-all duration-200">github.com/swokamoto</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>